  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures Mountain Goats performing at the Museum of Fine Arts on Friday, March 14, 2008 [1]. The setlist includes eighteen songs, beginning with “Marduk T-Shirt Men's Room Incident” and concluding with the encores “How to Embrace A Swamp Creature” and “No Children” [1]. Notable tracks include “New Zion,” which is the first in the archive, and “Sign of the Crow,” a rare performance with only three archived instances [1]. The group also plays “I Ain't Livin' Long Like This,” a Rodney Crowell cover that is mythic rare with just two archived performances [1]. The audio file is a FLAC transfer of a tape recorded by Peter Sohriakoff and transferred by Mike Wojciechowski [1]. It runs for 73 minutes and has received a perfect 5/5 rating from one listener [1]. A review of this specific recording by user thh200 describes it as a standout among the band's archived shows, specifically highlighting the performances of “Heretic Pride” and “Hast Thou Considered The Tetrapod” [2]. This concert is the 121st of 467 in the archive's collection for the band, following a previous show at NPR Soundcheck on March 11, 2008 [3]. The performance offers a complete look at the band's set that evening, including tracks like “Autoclave,” “New Monster Avenue,” and “Wild Sage” [1]. Listeners can expect a full experience of the band's catalog from this period, with the rare and first-in-archive tracks providing unique value [1]. The recording is the only available capture of this specific date and venue [1].",
